format: 2
name: any stops at the first match on both sides (T7, fixed)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 820500
expect: AGREE
note: The JVM returns true at 5 without dividing by 0; since ADR-070 D5 the script stops there too. Until then it also
note: evaluated 10 / 0 and failed (DIVERGE T7 Value/Failure).
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
import org.julclang.core.types.JulcList;

public class Probe {
    public static boolean m(JulcList<BigInteger> xs) {
        return xs.any(x -> BigInteger.TEN.divide(x).compareTo(BigInteger.ONE) > 0);
    }
}
